<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<configs>
	<!--
	  Resident behaviour, added to a member's AIPackages at RUNTIME by the mod (the list is rebuilt from the
	  entity class on every load, so it is re-added by the ticker). XNPCCore's utilityai.xml removes and
	  rebuilds /utility_ai/ai_packages, so this mod must load after it (folder name sorts after "0-").

	  A resident holds the Guard order (CurrentOrder 9): NPCModCore's Guard action walks them back to their
	  post and the combat packages (which only gate on NotHasOrder Stay) still fight anything that comes
	  close. These two actions add a daytime roam around the post and a quiet night, and ScDefendBase sends
	  them after an intruder they cannot see (M11 fix, "defend the base"); ScAtPost (M11 fix 2) lets them stand
	  at a post whose floor sits below the cell top, where Guard would re-plan for ever.

	  The roam, the leash and the quiet night are gated on ScIsResident (stationed at home), not merely on
	  membership: they work from the member's HOME post, and a FOLLOWER can hold the very same order 9 -
	  0-XNPCCore's "guard and return" voice order is buffOrderGuard. Such a follower guards where the player
	  said (NPCModCore's Guard) instead of being leashed back home from 500 m out.

	  A guard on watch (base defence D3, ScWatch: a resident whose post is a Watch post) stays put: ScNotOnWatch keeps
	  them out of the roam, the defence walk and hold, the quiet night (it would idle facing anywhere) and the Cowardly
	  flee, and - at the end of this file - out of 0-XNPCCore's two back-off actions and its melee approach. What is
	  left is Guard / ScAtPost (walk to the post, stand facing the post's way), the leash (measured from the Watch post,
	  never widened by a live attack) and the pack's attacks, which shoot or swing at whatever comes into range. These
	  gates and the DLL ship together: the consideration class lives in the DLL.
	-->
	<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages">
		<ai_package name="SCResident">
			<!-- ScRoamReady stays true while the roam runs and false for "cooldown" real seconds after it
			     stops; the AI re-scores every 0.2 s, so a cooldown consumed during scoring would end every
			     roam after one decision window. With ResidentRoamZone (blocks.xml; the default since round hz) radius and
			     cooldown are not used: the walk goes anywhere in the home zone, the resident stands ResidentRoamPauseMin..Max
			     seconds where it ended (the task still running, so Guard does not walk them back), and the next walk starts at
			     once (any gap would let Guard run them toward the post). -->
			<action name="ScRoam" weight="2.5" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="WanderHomeSC, SurvivorCommunity" radius="12" cooldown="45" />
				<consideration class="ScIsResident, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="EnemyNotNear, SCore" distance="30" />
				<consideration class="ScIsDaytime, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScRoamReady, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<!-- The leash. The pack's combat actions (weight 4-6) only stand down under a Stay order, so a
			     resident on Guard chases a zombie as far as it runs - playtest logs showed one 92 m from home.
			     This outscores the chase (but not point-blank self defence at weight 6) once they are further
			     from their post than ScConfig-independent "distance", walking them home with SCore's Guard task. With
			     ResidentRoamZone the home zone (and ResidentRoamZoneMargin round it) counts as home too. -->
			<action name="ScReturn" weight="5.5" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="Guard, SCore" />
				<consideration class="ScIsResident, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="ScFarFromPost, SurvivorCommunity" distance="25" />
			</action>
			<!-- Defend the base (M11 fix). Every combat action of the packs needs CanSeeTarget, and with a gun 0-XNPCCore's
			     SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced has no approach at all (its MeleeApproach is for CurrentWeaponClass 0), so a resident
			     stood at his post while a zombie walked through the base out of his sight. This walks him to any intruder
			     (ScIntruder: an awake enemy inside the home zone within DefendBaseRadius, 22 m, of his post (with ResidentRoamZone: of himself) - seen or not;
			     SCore's UAI scores every living entity in his bounds grown by his sight range, 60 m, i.e. about 30 m each
			     way, and sight is only a consideration, CanSeeTarget, left out here) for as long as he
			     cannot hit it from where he stands. ScCannotEngage: with a melee weapon beyond reach (NotInWeaponRange's
			     rule); with a gun out of range, without a clear shot (SCore's CanShoot ray: walls, glass, decor), or with
			     a friendly NPC in the line from farther than 6.5 m (closing in opens the line round the one in front); 0
			     the moment the gun is in range AND sees it, exactly RangedMeleeAttack's own pair, so the hand-over is
			     immediate (within 4.47 m, where SCore calls its attack target seen without a ray, SC casts it itself).
			     MoveToAttackTargetSDX paths to the entity with no sight test; it shoots nothing itself. ScIntruder also
			     pauses the defence for 20 s once the walk has taken him more than 23 m from his post (with ResidentRoamZone: 6 m outside the zone) (a detour round a
			     wall would otherwise trade turns with the 25 m leash every 0.2 s). Weight 4: beats Guard (2), ScRoam (2.5),
			     ScNightIdle (3) and BackupRanged (3); loses to every attack (5-7), the leash (5.5) and the Cowardly flee
			     (6), so the pack's own attack takes over the moment a shot or a swing is possible, and Guard walks him home
			     after. Ties MeleeApproach (4) with the same task; SCResident is the last package, so it wins the tie. A
			     Cowardly member ($Timid) does not go looking for a fight. Followers, runners and stand-ins: ScIsResident. -->
			<action name="ScDefendBase" weight="4" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="MoveToAttackTargetSDX, SCore" run="true" />
				<consideration class="ScIsResident, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasCVar, SCore" cvar="$Timid" value="1" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasBuff, SCore" buffs="SdcsIsHealing,buffHitStun" />
				<consideration class="ScIntruder, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScCannotEngage, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<!-- ...and holds still, facing the intruder, while his gun is in range with no block in the way but a player -
			     anywhere - or a friendly NPC within 6.5 m stands in the line (ScHoldFire): he never closes in on a fight
			     across you, and without this Guard walked him home and ScDefendBase walked him back. Its task also drops
			     the intruder as attack target, which SCore would otherwise treat as seen within 4.47 m whatever stands in
			     between (Patches_Npc's Patch_HoldFireAcross holds any such shot as well). The moment the line clears,
			     RangedMeleeAttack (6) fires; out of range, ScDefendBase walks on. Same weight and gates as ScDefendBase;
			     the two are never 1 for the same intruder, and on a tie between two intruders ScDefendBase, listed first,
			     wins (walking to one he can reach beats waiting on one he cannot shoot). -->
			<action name="ScDefendHold" weight="4" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="DefendHoldSC, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScIsResident, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasCVar, SCore" cvar="$Timid" value="1" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasBuff, SCore" buffs="SdcsIsHealing,buffHitStun" />
				<consideration class="ScIntruder, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScHoldFire, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<!-- A physical supply runner (ScRunners) holds the Task order (8), which nothing else in SCore or XNPCCore
			     uses: every resident action above stands down, the pack's combat still fires (it only gates on NotHasOrder
			     Stay), and this walks them along their route one waypoint at a time. 4.5 beats the chase (4) and idling,
			     and loses to in-range attacks (5-6), so a runner fights what reaches them and then walks on. -->
			<action name="ScTravel" weight="4.5" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="TravelSC, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScIsMember, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Task" />
				<consideration class="ScTravelling, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<!-- Following belongs to 0-XNPCCore: its DynamicFollow (NPCModNPCHired, weight 2) with Voice Control's
			     formations, follow distances and stances replaces the community's own follow (decision D6), and the
			     ticker reads every voice order as a member state. These two are only the FALLBACK for a member whose
			     packages have no DynamicFollow (ScNoDynamicFollow - a pack NPC from another mod): at 4 and 4.2 they
			     would outrank DynamicFollow and fight it. They were written for 3.1's pack, whose LeaderFollowSlow
			     (2) and TooCloseInside/Outside (3) made a follower orbit the player around 2.5 m: these walk the NPC
			     in to 3 m and let it stand. Combat (weight 4-6) still takes precedence. -->
			<action name="ScFollowLeader" weight="4" entity_filter="IsLeader">
				<task class="FollowSDX, SCore" stop_distance="3" max_distance="25" teleport_time="5" />
				<consideration class="ScIsMember, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNoDynamicFollow, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Follow" />
				<consideration class="TargetDistance" min="3" max="30" curve="threshold" />
			</action>
			<action name="ScHoldWithLeader" weight="4.2" entity_filter="IsLeader">
				<task class="IdleSDX, SCore" />
				<consideration class="ScIsMember, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNoDynamicFollow, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Follow" />
				<consideration class="EnemyNotNear, SCore" distance="20" />
				<consideration class="TargetDistance" flip_x="true" min="0" max="3" curve="threshold" />
			</action>
			<!-- At the post (M11 fix 2): within 0.8 m of it horizontally and 1.2 m of its floor the resident stands and faces
			     the post's look direction instead of running NPCModCore's Guard. Guard counts itself arrived only when the
			     floor of the body's height is the post's own cell, so on a surface below the cell top (a terrain surface, a
			     plate) it plans a path to where it already stands for ever, which the stuck watchdog took for a wedge.
			     Weight 2.2: beats Guard (2) only; loses to the roam (2.5), the quiet night (3), the defence (4), every attack
			     and the leash. -->
			<action name="ScAtPost" weight="2.2" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="HoldPostSC, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScIsResident, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="ScAtPost, SurvivorCommunity" xz="0.8" dy="1.2" />
			</action>
			<!-- only once they are back at the post: until then NPCModCore's Guard (weight 2) walks them home -->
			<action name="ScNightIdle" weight="3" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="IdleSDX, SCore" />
				<consideration class="ScIsResident, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="EnemyNotNear, SCore" distance="30" />
				<consideration class="ScIsNight, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNearPost, SurvivorCommunity" distance="4" />
			</action>
			<!-- Cowardly members ($Timid, written by ScTraits) run from enemies within 15 m. Up to 0-XNPCCore 3.1 its
			     NPCModCore had this very action; 3.2 commented it out ("$Timid has no writer" - this mod is one), so it
			     lives here now. NotHasOrder Stay keeps a parked, hidden runner or garrison body still. Under 3.1 both
			     run at the same weight, which is harmless. -->
			<action name="ScFlee" weight="6" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="FleeFromTarget" max_distance="30" />
				<consideration class="SelfHasCVar, SCore" cvar="$Timid" value="1" />
				<consideration class="NotHasOrder, SCore" order="Stay" />
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="TargetDistance" min="0" max="15" curve="threshold" />
				<consideration class="SelfVisible" />
			</action>
		</ai_package>

		<!-- Raiders (M10, DESIGN_M10_RAIDERS.md 2.7): SurvivorCommunity's hostile classes on 0-XNPCCore's player body run
		     NPCModCoreNoChat (idle, wander) and XNPC's SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced (the package that fires a vanilla gun or bow on
		     action 0, keeps its distance, and melees with the melee weapon), plus this package for the two things that one
		     lacks. Each action carries its own entity_filter, as SCore's hostile packages do. Both weigh less than the
		     attacks (5 to 7), so they only win when nothing can be shot or hit yet. -->
		<ai_package name="SCRaider">
			<!-- Close in on a seen enemy the gun or bow cannot reach yet: SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced's own approach is for the
			     melee weapon only (CurrentWeaponClass 0). -->
			<action name="ScRaiderApproach" weight="4" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="MoveToAttackTargetSDX, SCore" run="true" />
				<consideration class="NotHasOrder, SCore" order="Stay" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasCVar, SCore" cvar="CurrentWeaponClass" value="0" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasBuff, SCore" buffs="SdcsIsHealing,buffHitStun" />
				<consideration class="NotInWeaponRange, SCore" action_index="0" />
				<consideration class="CanSeeTarget, SCore" />
			</action>
			<!-- Heard, not seen: go and look, whatever is in the hand (SCore's hostile packages do this as MoveToFindTarget).
			     IsPlayer is any player, and every player is an enemy to a raider. -->
			<action name="ScRaiderInvestigate" weight="3" entity_filter="IsPlayer">
				<task class="MoveToInvestigate, SCore" run="true" />
				<consideration class="NotHasOrder, SCore" order="Stay" />
				<consideration class="CanNotSeeTarget, SCore" />
				<consideration class="CanHearTarget, SCore" />
				<consideration class="NotPathBlockedSDX, SCore" />
			</action>
		</ai_package>

		<!-- Enclave people (E2, Enclaves_Plan.md 2.3): added at spawn to every body of an enclave, survivor or raider
		     (ScEnclavePeople; a body is never saved, so it is never reloaded without it). SCResident action for action, aimed
		     at the enclave's POI instead of the home zone: the shared considerations and tasks resolve per body which ground it
		     has (UaiOps' ScHome / ScArea: a resident's post and the home zone, an enclave person's home spot and the POI's
		     footprint) - residents behave as before. Every action is gated on ScEncHome (the current body of an enclave's
		     person, at home, with a spot) instead of ScIsResident. They hold the Guard order at their spot (cvars written at
		     spawn, as Station does): NPCModCore's (or, for raiders, NPCModCoreNoChat's) Guard walks them back to it. A raider
		     enclave gets this too, so SCRaider's investigation and NPCModCoreNoChat's wander cannot pull it off its POI. -->
		<ai_package name="SCEnclave">
			<!-- the day roam over the POI (WanderHomeSC on the footprint, always the zone roam's walks and pauses) - never the
			     leader, who holds their spot so the player can find them -->
			<action name="ScEncRoam" weight="2.5" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="WanderHomeSC, SurvivorCommunity" radius="12" cooldown="45" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" role="member" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="EnemyNotNear, SCore" distance="30" />
				<consideration class="ScIsDaytime, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScRoamReady, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<!-- the leash: outside the POI by more than EnclaveLeashMargin (ScFarFromPost for an enclave person; "distance" is
			     the residents'), Guard walks them back to the spot. 5.5 outranks the packs' chase, as ScReturn does. -->
			<action name="ScEncReturn" weight="5.5" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="Guard, SCore" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="ScFarFromPost, SurvivorCommunity" distance="25" />
			</action>
			<!-- defend the POI: an awake enemy inside the footprint within EnclaveDefendRadius of the person, seen or not
			     (ScIntruder's enclave rule), with ScDefendBase's hand-overs to the packs' attacks -->
			<action name="ScEncDefend" weight="4" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="MoveToAttackTargetSDX, SCore" run="true" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasCVar, SCore" cvar="$Timid" value="1" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasBuff, SCore" buffs="SdcsIsHealing,buffHitStun" />
				<consideration class="ScIntruder, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScCannotEngage, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<action name="ScEncDefendHold" weight="4" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="DefendHoldSC, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasCVar, SCore" cvar="$Timid" value="1" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasBuff, SCore" buffs="SdcsIsHealing,buffHitStun" />
				<consideration class="ScIntruder, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScHoldFire, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</action>
			<!-- at the spot: stand facing its way (HoldPostSC, as ScAtPost) - the leader's place all day -->
			<action name="ScEncAtHome" weight="2.2" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="HoldPostSC, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="ScAtPost, SurvivorCommunity" xz="0.8" dy="1.2" />
			</action>
			<!-- the night: idle near the spot once Guard has walked them back to it -->
			<action name="ScEncNight" weight="3" entity_filter="IsSelf">
				<task class="IdleSDX, SCore" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="HasOrder, SCore" order="Guard" />
				<consideration class="EnemyNotNear, SCore" distance="30" />
				<consideration class="ScIsNight, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="ScNearPost, SurvivorCommunity" distance="4" />
			</action>
			<!-- the Cowardly ($Timid, their traits) run from enemies within 15 m -->
			<action name="ScEncFlee" weight="6" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="FleeFromTarget" max_distance="30" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="SelfHasCVar, SCore" cvar="$Timid" value="1" />
				<consideration class="NotHasOrder, SCore" order="Stay" />
				<consideration class="TargetDistance" min="0" max="15" curve="threshold" />
				<consideration class="SelfVisible" />
			</action>
			<!-- only for an enclave turned hostile (ScEncHostile: its grace over, not raiders - they carry SCRaider): SCRaider's
			     ranged approach and noise investigation, so a survivor with a gun closes in; still leashed by ScEncReturn -->
			<action name="ScEncApproach" weight="4" entity_filter="IsEnemy">
				<task class="MoveToAttackTargetSDX, SCore" run="true" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHostile, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="NotHasOrder, SCore" order="Stay" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasCVar, SCore" cvar="CurrentWeaponClass" value="0" />
				<consideration class="SelfNotHasBuff, SCore" buffs="SdcsIsHealing,buffHitStun" />
				<consideration class="NotInWeaponRange, SCore" action_index="0" />
				<consideration class="CanSeeTarget, SCore" />
			</action>
			<action name="ScEncInvestigate" weight="3" entity_filter="IsPlayer">
				<task class="MoveToInvestigate, SCore" run="true" />
				<consideration class="ScEncHostile, SurvivorCommunity" />
				<consideration class="NotHasOrder, SCore" order="Stay" />
				<consideration class="CanNotSeeTarget, SCore" />
				<consideration class="CanHearTarget, SCore" />
				<consideration class="NotPathBlockedSDX, SCore" />
			</action>
		</ai_package>
	</append>

	<!-- A guard on watch (D3) never backs off or walks to a melee target: on a tower either one walks them off the edge.
	     0-XNPCCore's SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced (weights 7, 3 and 4) gets one more consideration each; ScNotOnWatch is 1 for
	     everyone else, raiders and strangers included, so nothing changes for them. SC loads after 0-XNPCCore, whose
	     utilityai.xml builds this package. The melee swap itself is held off in the DLL (ScArms keeps a guard's gun). -->
	<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced']/action[@name='BackupKeepDistance']">
		<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
	</append>
	<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced']/action[@name='BackupRanged']">
		<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
	</append>
	<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced']/action[@name='MeleeApproach']">
		<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
	</append>

	<!--
	  0-XNPCCore 3.4 (game 3.4 only: its SdcsNpcCore package exists nowhere else, so on 3.2 nothing below applies).
	  Decision D1 (2026-10-29): everyone - members, prospects, enclave people, strangers - runs XNPC 3.4's own packages
	  (SdcsNpcCore, SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced, SdcsNpcHired, SdcsNpcMedic, SdcsNpcLoot, SdcsNpcLeave). Its new bands moved the
	  actions SC's were tuned against: Guard and Stay 2 -> 3, TooClose 3 -> 3.5, BackupRanged 3 -> 5, MeleeApproach 4 -> 5,
	  BackupKeepDistance 7 -> 8; new are the medic (7), the jobs and the leader's butchering (4), wild looting (1), leaving a
	  sleeper area an enemy hunts them in (9) and the busy animation (12). SC's actions are re-ranked so each keeps the place
	  it had among XNPC's on 3.2; XNPC's bands are not lowered, and its medic, jobs and leave-area are not gated (decision D1:
	  a resident may leave the post to heal, a member takes job orders, the leash and Guard bring them back after) - except
	  that enclave people at home never take the leave-area out of their own building (ScNotEncHome; the user, 2026-10-29).
	    ScAtPost, ScEncAtHome      2.2 -> 3.2  above Guard and Stay (3), still below the roam, the quiet night and TooClose
	                                           close in (3.5, scaled down with the distance)
	    ScRoam, ScEncRoam          2.5 -> 3.4  above the post (3.2) and Guard; TooClose still wins inside about 0.4 m
	    ScNightIdle, ScEncNight    3   -> 3.6  above TooClose's whole range, as 3 was above its 3; above the investigations
	    ScDefend*, ScEncDefend*    4   -> 5.2  above BackupRanged and MeleeApproach (5; the defence walk has the same task)
	                                           and MeleeAttack (5: never 1 together - ScCannotEngage is 0 in reach, and
	                                           ScHoldFire only answers for a gun); under the leash (5.5), the flee and the
	                                           shot (6), BackupKeepDistance (8) and the medic (7)
	    ScRaiderInvestigate,
	    ScEncInvestigate           3   -> 3.5  above the raised day roam and post, under the night idle (as 3 tied it and lost)
	    unchanged: ScReturn/ScEncReturn 5.5, ScFlee/ScEncFlee 6, ScTravel 4.5, ScRaiderApproach/ScEncApproach 4 (XNPC's
	    BackupRanged at 5 now backs a gun away from a close enemy it cannot shoot first - its 3.4 design, kept),
	    ScFollowLeader/ScHoldWithLeader (only for a pack NPC with no DynamicFollow, never one of XNPC's bodies).
	  ScTravel (4.5) cannot be placed by weight between MeleeApproach (5) and MeleeAttack (5): ScNotTravelling (1 unless the
	  NPC is a runner on the move) gates MeleeApproach and BackupRanged instead, so a runner walks on past what it sees and
	  still swings at what reaches it, as on 3.2.
	  NoActiveChat (Voice Control's own gate, which XNPC 3.4 put on Guard and Stay) on the post, the roam and the quiet night,
	  decision D8: while a dialog, trade or inventory window is open on the NPC or it is in a chat pause, Voice Control turns
	  it to the player and holds it - HoldPostSC's facing and the roam's walk would fight that every frame. The defence, the
	  leash and the flee keep running.
	-->
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsNpcCore&quot;]') != null">
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCResident']/action[@name='ScAtPost']/@weight">3.2</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCEnclave']/action[@name='ScEncAtHome']/@weight">3.2</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCResident']/action[@name='ScRoam']/@weight">3.4</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCEnclave']/action[@name='ScEncRoam']/@weight">3.4</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCResident']/action[@name='ScNightIdle']/@weight">3.6</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCEnclave']/action[@name='ScEncNight']/@weight">3.6</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCResident']/action[@name='ScDefendBase' or @name='ScDefendHold']/@weight">5.2</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCEnclave']/action[@name='ScEncDefend' or @name='ScEncDefendHold']/@weight">5.2</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCRaider']/action[@name='ScRaiderInvestigate']/@weight">3.5</set>
			<set xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCEnclave']/action[@name='ScEncInvestigate']/@weight">3.5</set>
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCResident']/action[@name='ScAtPost' or @name='ScRoam' or @name='ScNightIdle']">
				<consideration class="NoActiveChat, 1-XNPCVoiceControl" />
			</append>
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCEnclave']/action[@name='ScEncAtHome' or @name='ScEncRoam' or @name='ScEncNight']">
				<consideration class="NoActiveChat, 1-XNPCVoiceControl" />
			</append>
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced']/action[@name='MeleeApproach' or @name='BackupRanged']">
				<consideration class="ScNotTravelling, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
			<!-- the user, 2026-10-29: enclave people hold their ground inside their home when attacked - XNPC's leave-area
			     (9, over every fight) never walks one of them out of their own building -->
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcLeave']/action[@name='LeaveAreaSdcs']">
				<consideration class="ScNotEncHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>

	<!--
	  Round R1 (0-XNPCCore 3.4.02's bandits; SC's raiders are their children there, Config/entityclasses.xml): a band of
	  raiders on the road keeps walking. The bandits' HoldEngaged (3.5) stands, faces and targets any enemy within 40 m,
	  seen or not (SCore's utility AI scores every entity in see range), and beats Guard (3), the order a band walks by
	  (ScBands), so a band near zombies or an unseen player stopped and locked on. ScNotBandWalking is 0 for one of a
	  band's bodies while the band has not engaged the player, else 1 (everyone else: raiders in a den, wild raiders,
	  0-XNPCCore's own bandits). Their shot, swing and approach of what they see still run. Only where the action exists.
	-->
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsBanditCombat&quot;]/action[@name=&quot;HoldEngaged&quot;]/@name') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsBanditCombat']/action[@name='HoldEngaged']">
				<consideration class="ScNotBandWalking, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>

	<!--
	  C1 (round 22; 0-XNPCCore 3.4 only, the same guard): a resident on a work shift (ScWork) crafts through 0-XNPCCore's craft
	  order, which pins her with the Guard order at the craft spot (buffSdcsCraftHere) and runs CraftSdcsHere (4). SC's resident
	  roam (3.4), leash (5.5: it would drag her home from a station more than 25 m from her post), at-post (3.2) and quiet night
	  (3.6) all outrank 0-XNPCCore's Guard (3) and would walk her off it; ScNotOnShift (1 unless on a shift) keeps them out for
	  the shift. Her defence (5.2) and the Cowardly flee (6) stay: she fights for the base, then 0-XNPCCore's Guard brings her
	  back to the station and the item goes on.
	-->
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsNpcCore&quot;]') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SCResident']/action[@name='ScRoam' or @name='ScReturn' or @name='ScAtPost' or @name='ScNightIdle']">
				<consideration class="ScNotOnShift, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>

	<!--
	  Round 24 (H1; 0-XNPCCore 3.4.02 and later, only where each action exists): 0-XNPCCore's HoldEngaged - SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced
	  at 4, SdcsBanditCombat at 3.5 - stands the NPC facing any enemy within 40 m, seen or not, and never ends by itself. It
	  outranks every home action of SC's people (the post and the spot 3.2, the roams 3.4, the quiet nights 3.6, Guard 3), and
	  for an enemy outside the base nothing replaces it (the shot needs sight, the defence an intruder), so a resident stood
	  frozen facing zombies behind the walls. ScHoldEngagedHome is 1 for SC's home bodies (a resident: at the post, on watch
	  or on a work shift; an enclave's person at home) only when the target is an intruder by the base and enclave defence's
	  own rule (ScIntruder: an awake enemy inside the home zone or the enclave's footprint within the defend radius), else 0;
	  for everyone else - followers, strangers, plain 0-XNPCCore hires and bandits, SC's bands - it is 1. Appended last, after
	  0-XNPCCore's MayEngage and TargetDistance (and R1's ScNotBandWalking), which still run first. Their shots, the defence
	  and the bands' gate are untouched.
	-->
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced&quot;]/action[@name=&quot;HoldEngaged&quot;]/@name') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced']/action[@name='HoldEngaged']">
				<consideration class="ScHoldEngagedHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsBanditCombat&quot;]/action[@name=&quot;HoldEngaged&quot;]/@name') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsBanditCombat']/action[@name='HoldEngaged']">
				<consideration class="ScHoldEngagedHome, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>

	<!--
	  Round 25 (X2; 0-XNPCCore 3.4.03, only where each action exists).
	  - SdcsNpcCore's Flee (weight 9: $Timid, 15 m, sight) is live again in 3.4.03, with no Stay, watch or home gate and
	    above every SC action: a coward on a watch tower, a parked runner or an enclave's person at home would run.
	    ScNotScTimid is 0 for the bodies whose $Timid SC wrote (sc_timid), whose flight stays SC's gated ScFlee / ScEncFlee;
	    0-XNPCCore's own timid survivors keep this Flee.
	  - SdcsCover's TakeCover (6) and HoldEngaged's new retake walk (3.4.03: to cover up to 6 m from the guard post, through
	    doors) never take a guard on watch off the post: ScNotOnWatch (self only, as both actions allow).
	-->
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsNpcCore&quot;]/action[@name=&quot;Flee&quot;]/@name') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcCore']/action[@name='Flee']">
				<consideration class="ScNotScTimid, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsCover&quot;]/action[@name=&quot;TakeCover&quot;]/@name') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsCover']/action[@name='TakeCover']">
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>
	<conditional>
		<if cond="xpath('/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name=&quot;SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced&quot;]/action[@name=&quot;HoldEngaged&quot;]/@name') != null">
			<append xpath="/utility_ai/ai_packages/ai_package[@name='SdcsNpcRangedAdvanced']/action[@name='HoldEngaged']">
				<consideration class="ScNotOnWatch, SurvivorCommunity" />
			</append>
		</if>
	</conditional>
</configs>
